---
/**
 * /about/ — 소개 (CF-8 · US-8).
 *
 * REWRITTEN AGAIN 2026-09-07. This page is no longer the editorial charter;
 * it is the WRITER INTRODUCING THEMSELF. The three promises it used to put in
 * writing (실림 = 추천 / 미수록 ≠ 혹평 / 점수 = 순위) are gone from the site's
 * surfaces entirely — see 08-impl-notes/frontend.md for what that costs and
 * what no longer verifies them.
 *
 * THE COPY IS THE WRITER'S OWN AND IS REPRODUCED CHARACTER FOR CHARACTER.
 * Do not "fix" it. The spellings, the spacing, the missing full stop at the
 * end of the second paragraph and the line break inside the third are all as
 * written; they are a voice, not typos, and correcting them would replace
 * that voice with a copy editor's. Only the paragraph structure and the third
 * paragraph's internal break are typeset here.
 *
 * THE RIGHTS CONTACT LINE IS BACK (2026-09-07), at the foot of this page and
 * nowhere else. ADR-0008 lets this site publish album art it does not own on
 * three conditions — reduced copies only, sources recorded, and a way for a
 * rights holder to reach the publisher. Two rounds of deleting self-
 * describing copy took the third one off the site entirely, and a measurement
 * of the built output found the result: three streaming search links in the
 * whole site and not one repository link or mailto. A rights holder had no
 * route at all.
 *
 * WHY HERE AND NOT IN THE FOOTER. About is where a reader looks for who is
 * behind a site, and the footer links to it from every page — so the path is
 * one click from anywhere without putting a second sentence into the site
 * chrome, which is what this cycle has spent its time removing. It is one
 * line, it is quiet, and it is findable, which was the whole requirement.
 *
 * THE SECOND SENTENCE IS THE POINT, not politeness. "요청하시면 지체 없이
 * 내립니다" is what makes the door a request door: with it, a rights holder's
 * first contact is an email rather than a notice.
 *
 * Deliberately NOT inside .intro — that section is the writer's own three
 * paragraphs, verbatim, and browser.flows.spec.ts counts them.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

import { SITE_TAGLINE } from '../lib/site.ts';
---

<Base title="About" description={SITE_TAGLINE} path="/about/" current="about">
  <main class="about">
    {/* No overline. The masthead vocabulary puts an English section name
        above a DIFFERENT heading; "About" over "About" would print the same
        word twice, which is the duplicate-title problem this round removed
        from the finalized list page. A bare English h1 is what every other
        utility page here already uses. */}
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

    <section class="intro">
      <p>그저 음악이 좋아서 매일 이어폰을 꼽고 사는 평범한 음악 팬입니다.</p>
      <p>전문적인 지식이나 글쓰는 솜씨는 부족하지만<br />음악을 향한 진심을 담아 쉬운 언어로 가볍고 편안하게 음악을 소개하겠습니다.</p>
      <p>시대를 넘나드는 위대한 명반부터<br />갓 나온 신보까지 언제든 편하게 들러 같이 만나요.</p>
    </section>

    {/* ADR-0008 §4. The URL is a literal because config/ is data the editor
        owns and this is a property of the code's home, not of the
        publication; a repo move is a one-line edit here. */}
    <footer class="rights">
      <p>
        앨범 커버 등 권리 문의는 <a href="https://github.com/fgda114/undernote/issues" rel="noopener">저장소 이슈</a>로
        연락해 주세요. 요청하시면 해당 이미지는 지체 없이 내립니다.
      </p>
      {/* Font attribution. The OFL does not require a notice on the PAGE —
          it requires the licence to travel with the font files, which is what
          licenses/ does — so this line is a credit, not compliance, and it is
          one sentence for that reason. It sits beside the rights-contact line
          because both answer "whose work is on this page that is not the
          writer's", and that question has exactly one place to be answered. */}
      <p>
        본문 서체는 <a href="https://github.com/orioncactus/pretendard" rel="noopener">Pretendard</a>와
        <a href="https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk" rel="noopener">Noto Serif KR</a>입니다 — 둘 다 SIL Open Font License 1.1.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    width: min(var(--shell), 100% - 2 * var(--gutter));
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: var(--s-48) 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-32);
  }
  /* TITLE→CONTENT IS THE SITE'S ONE SHARED GAP, --s-24, NOT THIS PAGE'S OWN
     --s-32 (2026-09-08). Same fix, same reasoning, as archive/index.astro's
     identical rule: `.about`'s 32px `gap` is this page's own rhythm between
     .intro and the .rights colophon below it, which stays untouched; only
     the title, as the flex column's first item, was borrowing that number
     for a different question (title-to-content) it was never meant to
     answer. Margins on a flex item stack with `gap` rather than collapsing
     into it, so 32px + this rule's −8px lands the ONE pair this page shares
     with every other tab (title → first content) on the same 24px. Scoped to
     this page — global.css's shared `.page-title` rule is untouched. */
  .page-title {
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--s-24) - var(--s-32));
  }
  /* Reading size, reading measure, ordinary paragraph rhythm. The previous
     version set these lines at 27px/800 with a left rule, which asserted them
     at the reader; this copy is someone saying hello and is typeset that way.
     Sans, not serif — the serif belongs to review bodies and the annual
     preface (§5.1), and this is neither. */
  .intro {
    max-width: var(--column);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-24); /* the running-prose paragraph gap, untouched by the density pass */
    color: var(--ink-prose);
    font-size: var(--fs-17);
    line-height: 1.85;
  }
  /* Set at the page's smallest text size in --muted: this is a notice, not
     something the reader came for, and it should read as the colophon it is.
     The link keeps the site's link grammar — --accent-2-ink plus an underline,
     never colour alone (WCAG 1.4.1) — because a contact path nobody
     recognises as clickable is the same as no contact path. */
  .rights {
    max-width: var(--column);
    font-size: var(--fs-13);
    line-height: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    /* Two notices now (rights contact, font credit). Flex + gap rather than
       paragraph margins so the block's spacing comes from the scale and a
       third notice needs no new rule. --s-12 keeps them reading as one
       colophon: the .intro gap above is twice this, which is what separates
       "the writer's prose" from "the small print". */
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-12);
  }
  .rights a {
    color: var(--accent-2-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .rights a:hover {
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .about {
      padding-top: var(--s-32);
    }

    .intro {
      font-size: var(--fs-16);
      line-height: 1.8;
    }
  }
</style>
